      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects offered in the academic year 2024: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- total of 12 units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- Mathematics department (Course 18): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject code: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\n- subject title: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- school name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- number of such subjects offered in that school: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\n- variance of the total units of courses offered by that department: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- courses with a non-null total units value: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n\n## Join Keys\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and rank within each school name group ordered by subject code.\n```sql\nSELECT t1.SUBJECT_CODE, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.SCHOOL_NAME, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t0.SCHOOL_NAME ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_CODE) AS window_column FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024 AND t1.TOTAL_UNITS = 12 AND t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\n```\n2. For each department, what is the department name, and what are the variance and standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department, considering only courses with a non-null total units value and departments that grant degrees, specifically for the Mathematics department (Course 18)?\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS variance_total_units, STDDEV(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS stddev_total_units FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG ccc ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccc.TOTAL_UNITS IS NOT NULL GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ;\n```\n3. For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and, for each school, the number of such subjects offered in that school. Only include schools where at least 2 such subjects are offered.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t1.SUBJECT_CODE, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.SCHOOL_NAME FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024 AND t1.TOTAL_UNITS = 12 AND t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' ) SELECT ic.SUBJECT_CODE, ic.SUBJECT_TITLE, ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.SCHOOL_NAME, sc.subject_count FROM inner_cte ic JOIN ( SELECT SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(*) AS subject_count FROM inner_cte GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME HAVING COUNT(*) >= 2 ) sc ON ic.SCHOOL_NAME = sc.SCHOOL_NAME ORDER BY ic.SCHOOL_NAME, ic.SUBJECT_CODE;\n```\n4. For each department that grants degrees, what is the department name, and what are the variance and standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department, considering only courses with a non-null total units value, and also show the school name for each department?\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS variance_total_units, STDDEV(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS stddev_total_units FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG ccc ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccc.TOTAL_UNITS IS NOT NULL GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.variance_total_units, ic.stddev_total_units, sd.SCHOOL_NAME FROM inner_cte ic JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME = sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and, for each school, the number of such subjects offered in that school (only including schools where at least 2 such subjects are offered), and also show the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses with a non-null total units value and only for degree-granting departments), and only include results where the department name and school name match in both sets of criteria. List the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, subject count, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units. Do not return any rounded answers."
