      "content": "The MySQL connection is persistently returning an authentication error (`Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`), so runtime verification is not possible in this session. I will therefore rely on the semantic-network evidence and the documented precedent SQL, which fully determine the query shape.\n\n---\n\n# Investigation Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated in full):**\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — department dimension, one row per academic department. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (join key), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` ('Mathematics'), `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'). The only dimension carrying both school attribution and the degree-granting flag (per `concept_department_dimension` comparisons).\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — warehouse course catalog fact, one row per subject offering per term/academic year. Carries `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `SUBJECT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`. Per `concept_course_catalog_sources` decision guide: \"Default choice for unit statistics… of subjects.\"\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG** — alternative CIS catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure, keyed by academic year/term/subject; carries `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `TOTAL_UNITS`.\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION** — course descriptions with `DEPARTMENT` (= SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (course-level flag), `COURSE_LEVEL`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED** — registrar offering/enrollment fact tables (subject rollup / subject-cluster summary / section grain). They carry enrollment measures; SUBJECT_OFFERED has no unit measures.\n- **DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG** — third catalog feed with SO_* links to registrar offerings.\n- **STUDENT_DEPARTMENT** — lighter department lookup (code, name, full name, school) without `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`.\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE** — subject-code lookup (code → description, department, school).\n\n**Metrics:** dw_1471, dw_2210, dw_1758, dw_3248, dw_1393, dw_1023, dw_1049, dw_3311, dw_2151, dw_1335, dw_2272, dw_1212, dw_2335, dw_41, dw_104, dw_359, dw_3644, dw_2958, dw_4756, dw_5150 — all retrieved in full (SQL inspected).\n\n**Concepts:** concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_department_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts — full comparisons and decision guides retrieved.\n\n**Column concepts:** column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_year_columns — full details retrieved.\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED graph neighbors: joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT_CODE), SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL), FCLT_ROOMS, CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE, SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE; incoming joins from CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), TIP/LIBRARY tables. Concept memberships: concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources. Column concepts: total_units, department_name, subject_id, term_code, year_columns, hass_attribute.\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG joins to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_ID) and to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE/SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE (documented in hint join keys and used in dw_1335, dw_2272, dw_2335 precedents).\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE (used in dw_1393, dw_1212, dw_4756).\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Catalog source matrix** (evidence: concept_course_catalog_sources comparisons):\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | CIS_COURSE_CATALOG | DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Source | Warehouse catalog fact | CIS feed | Drupal feed |\n| Distinctive cols | MEET_PLACE, RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY, EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE | Same attribute set, no MEET_PLACE/MEET_TIME | SO_* registrar links |\n| Documented usage | \"Default choice for unit statistics\" | \"Used when subject titles must be resolved through SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\" | Tied to registrar records |\n\n**3b. Task-requirement fitness:**\n- \"subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units\" + SUBJECT_CODE/SUBJECT_TITLE/DEPARTMENT_NAME → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (has ACADEMIC_YEAR, TOTAL_UNITS, SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_TITLE, DEPARTMENT_NAME — verified in columns). Precedent dw_1471/dw_1758 use exactly `ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024 AND TOTAL_UNITS = 12 AND DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'` on this table.\n- \"school name\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME: SUPPORTED (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED has no school column; hint join key DEPARTMENT_CODE↔DEPARTMENT_CODE; dw_1471 precedent joins exactly this way).\n- \"variance/STDDEV of total units of courses offered by that department… degree-granting… non-null total units\" → CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS + SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING: SUPPORTED per hint column mapping and precedents dw_1335/dw_2272/dw_2335 (all compute CIS_COURSE_CATALOG unit stats with `TOTAL_UNITS IS NOT NULL` and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' on SIS_DEPARTMENT).\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT for school name: NOT-SUPPORTED for the degree-granting criterion (no IS_DEGREE_GRANTING column, per concept_department_dimension comparison).\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY as the AY2024 12-unit source: NOT-SUPPORTED for the wording \"subjects offered in the academic year 2024\" — they are term-keyed registrar tables without ACADEMIC_YEAR; column_concept_year_columns decision guide says group by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR for \"academic year YYYY\" offering questions.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-field anchoring:** \"Mathematics department (Course 18)\" → `DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'` (domain-knowledge hint; dw_1471/dw_1758 precedent). \"number of such subjects offered in that school… at least 2\" → COUNT over the filtered subject set grouped by SCHOOL_NAME with HAVING COUNT(*) >= 2 (hint subquery 3). \"match in both sets of criteria\" → join the subject set to the department-stats set on DEPARTMENT_NAME and SCHOOL_NAME.\n\n**3d. Precedent usage evidence:** AY2024+12units+Mathematics on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED⋈SIS_DEPARTMENT: 2 precedents (dw_1471, dw_1758). CIS_COURSE_CATALOG TOTAL_UNITS variance/STDDEV with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING and NOT NULL filter: 3 precedents (dw_1335, dw_2272, dw_2335). COURSE_CATALOG-based variance/STDDEV: dw_1471, dw_1023, dw_41. The hint's column mapping explicitly assigns \"variance/standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department\" to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS.\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: consumed by ~all catalog-unit metrics (dw_1471, dw_1758, dw_104, dw_41, dw_1023, dw_2151, dw_3248…); serves \"which subjects with X units in year Y\" patterns.\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG: consumed by dw_1335, dw_2272, dw_2335, dw_3311, dw_2210 for alternative-feed unit dispersion statistics.\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: universal dimension for school/degree-granting filters (dw_1471, dw_2151, dw_1212, dw_2272…).\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION: course-level degree-granting/level attributes (dw_1393, dw_4756, dw_1758).\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: SIS_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (semantic_get); concepts concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_department_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts (semantic_get); column concepts total_units, department_name, subject_id, year_columns (semantic_get); metrics dw_1471, dw_2210, dw_1393, dw_3311, dw_1758, dw_3248, dw_1023, dw_1049, dw_2151, dw_1335, dw_2272, dw_1212, dw_2335, dw_41, dw_104, dw_359, dw_3644, dw_2958, dw_4756, dw_5150 (semantic_get); graph traversal on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (semantic_graph). mysql_query attempted repeatedly — all attempts failed with an authentication error, so data-level verification was not possible.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT_CODE) for the AY2024 12-unit Mathematics subjects with school name; count per SCHOOL_NAME with HAVING ≥ 2; compute VARIANCE/STDDEV over CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT_CODE) filtered by IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' and TOTAL_UNITS IS NOT NULL, grouped by DEPARTMENT_NAME/SCHOOL_NAME; join the two sets on DEPARTMENT_NAME and SCHOOL_NAME.\n\n**6b.** CTE structure: `inner_cte` (subjects) → `school_counts` (HAVING COUNT(*)>=2) → `dept_stats` (variance/stddev) → final join. Bare STDDEV() per the tip. No rounding.\n\n**6c.** Data perspective: all required columns physically exist (verified via retrieved column definitions); DEPARTMENT_CODE joins are documented 1:1 dimension keys (no fan-out). Semantic-network perspective: concept decision guides designate COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED as default catalog source and SIS_DEPARTMENT as the school/degree-granting dimension; hint column mapping assigns the variance/stddev measure to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS. Business perspective: dw_1471/dw_1758 use the identical AY2024+12units+Math filter; dw_1335/dw_2272/dw_2335 use the identical CIS_COURSE_CATALOG non-null-units + degree-granting dispersion pattern; hint subqueries 2–4 give the exact decomposition.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: computing variance/STDDEV from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED instead (dw_1471 precedent) — rejected because the hint's column mapping explicitly anchors \"variance/standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department\" to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS with the non-null filter, matching dw_3311/dw_2335 wording (\"courses offered by that department… non-null total units\").\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
